{title: Wabash Cannonball}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
From the [C]great Atlantic Ocean to the [F]wide Pacific [C]shore,
From the [C]queen of flowing mountains to the [G7]south belt by the [G7]shore.
She's [C]mighty tall and handsome and [F]known quite well by [C]all,
She's the [C]regular combination of the [G7]Wabash Cannon[C]ball.

{c: Chorus}
Listen [C]to the jingle, the [F]rumble and the [C]roar,
As she [C]glides along the woodland, through the [G7]hills and by the [G7]shore.
Hear the [C]mighty rush of the engine, hear the [F]lonesome hobo [C]call,
You're [C]traveling through the jungle on the [G7]Wabash Cannon[C]ball.

{c: Verse 2}
Our [C]eastern states are dandy, so the [F]people always [C]say,
From [C]New York to St. Louis and [G7]Chicago by the [G7]way.
From the [C]hills of Minnesota where the [F]rippling waters [C]fall,
No [C]chances can be taken on the [G7]Wabash Cannon[C]ball.
